{"_id":"6a2ff4e72204ffbc59e5a5a4","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"wxO7f8wh6JTXHYDiPcbmy","description":"# Filtering & Querying\n\nFiltering in Pandas selects rows that meet specified conditions. Boolean masks, the `.query()` method, and `.isin()` are common approaches. Multiple conditions can be combined with `&` (and) and `|` (or), and the `.query()` method allows SQL-like string syntax for readable filtering expressions.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"pandas.DataFrame.query","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.DataFrame.query.htmlme.query","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb38"},{"type":"official","title":"How do I select a subset of a DataFrame?","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/getting_started/intro_tutorials/03_subset_data.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb39"},{"type":"article","title":"10 Elegant Ways to Filter Pandas DataFrames","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/stop-writing-messy-boolean-masks-10-elegant-ways-to-filter-pandas-dataframes/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb3a"},{"type":"video","title":"Filtering Columns and Rows in Pandas","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kB7FV-ijdqE","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb3b"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:49:43.727Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/wxO7f8wh6JTXHYDiPcbmy.md"}